# Data conversion between byte and tebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between byte and tebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1B to 0.0000TiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5B yields 0.0000TiB; backward, converting 1TiB to 1099511627776B preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5TiB yields 1649267441664.0B. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1B
print(forward_whole->to(TiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5B
print(forward_fractional->to(TiB))
backward_whole: int = 1TiB
print(backward_whole->to(B))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TiB
print(backward_fractional->to(B))

<<< stdout
0.0000TiB
0.0000TiB
1099511627776B
1649267441664.0B

<<< stderr
